TEXT 0 -224 Left 2 ;Second-order band-stop or notch (output on the series LC): H(s) = (s² + ω0²) / (s² + s ω0/Q + ω0²)\nω0 = 1/√(LC) = 31.6 krad/s (f0 ≈ 5.03 kHz) and Q = √(L/C) / R ≈ 2.1: two complex poles at −ω0/2Q ± jω0√(1 − 1/4Q²).\nThe zeros are on the jω axis, at ±jω0: at f0 the LC is a short circuit and the output is 0. Bode: 0 dB far from f0 and a deep notch at f0, where the phase jumps 180°.\nStep: out jumps to 1 (at first L is an open circuit), dips with a damped ring and goes back to 1.
